# Triumph Stag two-door coupe, 1970-1977.
#
# The V8-engined Stag, with the permanent T-bar, the polished uprights and the
# four-lamp grille. Modelled with the factory hardtop fitted, because that is the
# closed body the pack's other cars are built as: the flank comes from a soft-top
# photograph, and the hardtop roofline, C-pillar and rear panel from two hardtop
# views. Federal side markers and bumper additions are not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triumph_Stag
#
# Dimensions 4.394 x 1.613 x 1.257 m, wheelbase 2.540 m, from the English
# Wikipedia Stag specifications. Handles take the modelled width to 1.641 m.
#
# Colours are Triumph's own, from the Stag specialist's annual colour tables, and
# this is the best paint evidence of any Triumph model in the batch:
#   Damson          1971 and 1972 model years
#   Sapphire        1972 model year
#   Saffron         1971 and 1972 model years
#   White           1971 and 1972 model years
# The tables are secondary originality research rather than a period chart
# inspected here, and they disagree with themselves in places; only the years
# above are used. Weights damson 3, white 3, saffron 2, sapphire 2, total 10,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 195 km/h for the 3.0 V8, a step below the car's quoted maximum because
# the Stag's gearing and the period tyres did not encourage sustained running.
# Comfort 100/480, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 100: a soft, well-trimmed GT, a step
# above the Spitfire. Classes 1,2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: June 1970 intro, retires staggered 1990-1993 on a
# thirteen- to twenty-three-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/triumph-stag.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/triumph-stag.dae (53 objects). References:
# citycars/references/triumph-stag/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the shoulders and the lower front and rear panels are more
# angular than the photographs. At 128 px the low hardtop roofline, the two-door
# cabin, the T-bar and the four-lamp nose read as the Stag.

obj=citycar
name=TriumphStag(Damson)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1970
intro_month=6
retire_year=1993
retire_month=6
speed=195
length=3
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=100
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=480

Image[E]=./images/triumph-stag-damson_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/triumph-stag-damson_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/triumph-stag-damson_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/triumph-stag-damson_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/triumph-stag-damson_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/triumph-stag-damson_NW.0.0,12,10
